In case you want to remix the image, after chaning what you want, you will need the scripts i used to make a diff between the original image from Microsoft and yours. Here are the scripts i used to generate the files_to_delete and slim the image:

./generate_list.sh ./full ./slim files_to_delete

After generating the list, you slim the image accouding to it before repackaging (so that directories full and slim become identical)

./clean_dir.sh files_to_delete ./full

Or, to remove the lot of now empty directories

./clean_dir_emptydir.sh files_to_delete ./full

Note: the wim images will almost never be byte or hash identical, since Microsoft, in its infinite wisdom, made the format so that the metadata about the generation dir and total file size etc. are inside the image and thus change it.
